/-
AtFullSide/K1/OpeningLookK4.lean: THE SHARED "SENDING" (the kind K1): BEHIND THE SHORT LEMMA FROM
THE CUT TO THE LOOK (msgTxt_mask_look_one, Johnson/Desc/ProofFile/Honest/K1/Law/LookOfCut.lean): ITS
TWO CALLS AT THE OPENING's JOB, AT MESSAGE 0 (the mask row) AND AT MESSAGE 4 (the index masks'
message), UNDER THE LIBRARY's HEAD h AND AN OPENING O: THE ADDRESS AND THE NUMBER WRITTEN IN THE
SPENDER's TERMS (rowZeroW, rawIdxW, K4's k4IndexRow, k4IndexPlace, k4IndexTakes) BY EQUATIONS ON
PLANS, SHAPES AND WRITTEN VALUES; AND THE SAME TWO WITH THE OPENING STRUCK, AT A RETURNED onlineProverFromPublicFiles.
Four theorems and one tool; no definition.

THE RIDER, WITH EVERY QUOTATION OF ANY OF THE FOUR.
An identity of two readings of one element, at each run's coins: it says WHICH element of the run
the entry is. It says nothing on how that element is drawn, on who else reads or spends it, or that
it stands at no other entry. Of hE, "the key", it is the whole, in hE's own signs, at K1's opening's
job, under the head and an opening: for row 2 as it stands, for row 1 with rowZeroW for row. It pays
hE in no tie until that tie's top calls it.
(The two forms that end in _at take hA, "onlineProverFromPublicFiles returns A", in the opening's stead.)

  ride_zero_four     a tool: members 0 and 4 of rides_first_written: no table rides there
  opening_look_row   (P1) what msgTxt answers at (true, 0, nu) of message 0, nu below rows * length,
                     is the look's element number rowZeroW.base.e + nu at rowZeroW.owner
  opening_look_idx   (P2) at g below 12: what msgTxt answers at K4's row and place of message 4 is
                     the look's element number rawIdxW.base.e + k4IndexTakes Zp g at rawIdxW.owner
  opening_look_row_at, opening_look_idx_at   the same two ends; O struck; hA in its stead; hJ said
                     at the returned prover's own ground A.G and public part A.Z

For whom. The premise hE, "the key", of K4's two ties at the joined Script (on no list).
opening_look_idx ends in row 2's hE sign for sign; opening_look_row in row 1's with
rowZeroW for row and rows * length of message 0 for L. THAT row IS rowZeroW IS NOT SAID HERE. Their
named callers: the two tops that K4's house types over its ties.

THE OPENING, STRUCK. w_at_mg (Johnson/Desc/Kinds/Law/K6StateAtHead.lean) gives an opening from the
head alone, as an existence; atPure_at_laid_ground (Honest/AtHeadGround.lean) at Open.blank of that
opening (Johnson/IMR/SeatOpen.lean: blankBy pureRoad.links Zp = some Bs.G₀) ties its ground to the
returned prover's: A.Z = Zp and A.G = Bs.G₀: AND SO AT ANY OPENING AT Zp: Open.blank says what one
function returns at Zp, so two openings have one ground; and Open.unique (the same file) says it of
all their letters: they are functions of the three files. So the two _at forms name no Bs: hJ stands
in the spelling of hasCoins_two_at_book (Honest/K1/Law/HasCoinsAtBook.lean), which pays hasCoins at
A.B under the same h, hA and hJ. WHEN THAT IS A PAYMENT IN A TIE, on (c)
below: PROVIDED the tie's top takes O out of that law itself and hJ is said at the ground that this
very opening returns, so that nobody can lay another opening beside it.

WHAT LIES BEFORE hE CEASES TO BE A PREMISE THAT NOBODY PAYS: SIX THINGS ((P1) = opening_look_row,
(P2) = opening_look_idx):


  (a) (P1) (P2) through Lean
  
  (b) K4's TOPS through Lean WITH NO hE AMONG THEIR PREMISES: at the tops, not at (P1) (P2)
  
  (c) what comes INTO the ties with them, by name: no tie of the second form takes an opening or
  names placeJob [by program: 0 · 0]: so O, and "the list's job is the opening's placeJob" (hJ,
  with hx, and hn at n = 0 | 4), are NEW premises there: an exchange, unless O is had from h and hAt
  (d) "row = rowZeroW" for row 1
  (e) the fourteen files as rows, or told as no rows beside every quotation
  (f) all of it anew over the eleventh.

THE FOURTEEN FILES THAT ARE NO ROWS OF laws.12, TOLD WITH EVERY QUOTATION: this one;
Honest/K1/Law/LookOfCut; beneath them AtFullSide/K1/OpeningStartsW, OpeningLengthsW, OpeningSeatsK4,
SegmentZeroAtWritten, SegmentZeroJoints, MergeRowAtWritten; Honest/K1/Law/RowOwnerAtWritten,
MaskStartIsBook, DueIsBook, StartAtFour; and two of K4's house: Honest/K4/Lot/IndexNum, MaskNum.

hasCoins. At a book whose count at the part's address does not cover the part's due this law holds
for nothing, and it is never quoted as if it spoke there: hasCoins is neither asked nor paid here:
whoever quotes this law at a book names hasCoins at that book beside it.
The book is a letter. "= some" carries that the book COVERS the due, no more. That the premise is
not idle: msgTxt_answers (Honest/K1/LotsLaid.lean) under hasCoins at a book.

sendFits. No premise: no step spends it. Whoever quotes either law names sendFits at the opening's
plan beside it (why: LookOfCut.lean's head): at the written plan it is fits_first_written
(Honest/K1/Law/FitsWritten.lean).

The road. hJ gives the job's plan and, by placeJob_ride, its ride. msgTxt_mask_look_one at n = 0 |
4: hn: openingNos_head; hr: ride_two_head, then ride_zero_four (which calls range_at,
Honest/K2/Law/Reads.lean); h1: opening_head; hnu: the premise | idxTakes_below, with 1 * length =
length. The ends: opening_head_written, read from right to left. K4's row and place: idxEntry_head,
with nu % 1 = 0 and nu / 1 = nu. The _at forms: w_at_mg at h.toAtMg; atPure_at_laid_ground at
h.laid, O.blank and hA; then the form with O, hJ rewritten by the two equations.

Limits. h AND O (IN THE _at FORMS: h AND hA) ARE PREMISES: where there is no such head, opening or
returned onlineProverFromPublicFiles they hold for nothing. THE FULL SIZE ALONE; the format's second hash function alone.
opening_look_idx at g from 12 on, opening_look_row at nu from rows * length on: nothing is said. NOT
SAID: that any text answers; that the lot's number is K4's. An identity at each run's coins. Nothing
on any property.
Terms: lean/GLOSSARY.md.
-/
import AtFullSide.K1.OpeningSeatsK4
import AtFullSide.K1.OpeningStartsW
